index 0000000..7def5f5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/RELEASE-V16.97.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+JTMOS V68.8.57.10.18.16.97 - GeForce 6150SE/MCP61 native LFB modeset
+2026-09-05
+
+Target hardware
+---------------
+Acer/eMachines systems using NVIDIA GeForce 6150SE nForce 430 / MCP61,
+PCI ID 10DE:03D0.
+
+Changes
+-------
+* Adds kernel32/drivers/vga/nv6150.c/.h.
+* Early PCI probe finds 10DE:03D0 and discovers BAR0 MMIO + BAR1 LFB.
+* BAR1 is connected to the existing JTMOS VESA/LFB paging contract before
+  paging is enabled, while VGA text remains visible.
+* VBE-first policy is retained: a valid boot32 VBE handoff always wins.
+* If VBE is unavailable, the NVIDIA provider is tried before VBox/BGA.
+* Native CRTC0 modes supported initially:
+    - 1024x768x32 @ 60 Hz for GraOS
+    - 640x480x32 @ 60 Hz recovery mode
+* Programs NV4x/Curie VGA CRTC extensions, PCRTC scanout, PRAMDAC packed-pixel
+  state, C61 FIFO arbitration and the two-stage VPLL.
+* C61 two-stage PLL follows the legacy Linux nvidiafb model: first-stage VCO
+  400..1000 MHz, P:N:M in VPLL A and fixed 0x80000401 second stage.
+* Compile-time recovery switch NV6150_NATIVE_PLL=0 refuses native mode changes
+  while retaining probe/LFB preparation.
+* Adds tools/check_nv6150_lfb.sh and docs/NVIDIA-6150SE-MCP61.md.
+
+Safety / scope
+--------------
+The driver deliberately does not re-route outputs, program TV/LVDS/TMDS,
+accelerate 2D/3D, or implement dual-head/EDID/DDC.  It preserves BIOS analog
+routing and only changes display registers when GraOS explicitly requests the
+native graphics transition after paging is active.
+
+Hardware validation
+-------------------
+The source and mode/PLL arithmetic are regression-tested and the changed kernel
+objects compile with the JTMOS IA-32/Linode profile.  Final visual validation
+must be performed on the eMachines GeForce 6150SE machine.
